From e1fcb142be44c218b4d2db6ebb0ba9b2d8a485ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:50:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Query service: the user's token to the adapter, and a
 completeness banner

The otel-chdb fork's ClickHouse connection is the query service's HyperDX
adapter (otel-chdb/query, cmd/hdxadapter), which runs every statement
through POST /v1/query scoped to the caller's OIDC token and returns the
result's completeness label in X-Otel-* response headers.

- api: the ClickHouse proxy forwards the user's token, from the header the
  OIDC proxy in front of HyperDX sets (HDX_QUERY_SERVICE_TOKEN_HEADER, e.g.
  x-forwarded-access-token), as Authorization: Bearer. Only that header;
  anything that is not a single token is not forwarded. Unset: upstream
  behaviour.
- common-utils (node client: alerts, the API's own queries, MCP): a token
  from HDX_QUERY_SERVICE_TOKEN_FILE, re-read per query (rotation without a
  restart), sent as the query's `auth` ({access_token}: Authorization:
  Bearer); a per-query http_headers Authorization would be overwritten by
  the client's Basic header. An empty file is an error, never a query
  without a token.
- common-utils: clickhouse/completeness.ts. Every result's label is recorded
  under its statement text (a refresh replaces its own label); a result
  without one is "unlabelled", never complete; schema answers are not
  recorded. One store per tab (on globalThis, whatever the bundle).
- app: CompletenessBanner above every page: "Complete through T", "Partial:
  data from T on may still arrive", "Unknown - watermark stale", "Unknown -
  not labelled". The worst label of the page's results; reset on navigation.
- metadata: a failed mergeTreeTextIndex key lookup (the service refuses
  table functions: the index's tokens are every cluster's) falls through to
  the rollup and scan paths instead of returning an empty key list.
- Fixes patch 0001's clickhouse.test.ts: one default-settings expectation
  missed the pinned overflow modes.
